  "name": "Disguised Casting (Su)",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "subType": "classFeat",
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> —</p><p>An illusionist can spend 1 point from his veil pool as a free action while casting an illusion spell to disguise his spellcasting. Creatures attempting to identify the spell as it is being cast must succeed at a Will save (DC 10 + half of the illusionist's level + his Charisma modifier) or misidentify the spell as a spell of the illusionist's choice. The illusory spell must be the same level as the true spell, but can be any spell he has seen cast before.</p>",
